  <strong|Evidence.> <hlink|<verbatim|YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/Bubbles.lean:14\U26>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/Bubbles.lean#L14-L26>,
  <hlink|<verbatim|YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/Bubbles.lean:48\U61>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/Bubbles.lean#L48-L61>,
  <hlink|<verbatim|YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/Bubbles.lean:125\U141>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/Bubbles.lean#L125-L141>
  derives color traces and the vector/ghost integrand.
  <hlink|<verbatim|YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/MomentumIntegral.lean:326\U338>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/MomentumIntegral.lean#L326-L338>,
  <hlink|<verbatim|YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/MomentumIntegral.lean:346\U408>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Next/STATIONARY/OneLoop/MomentumIntegral.lean#L346-L408>
  integrates the pole and controls the remaining terms.
  <hlink|<verbatim|YM/Next/STATIONARY/FullPlanned.lean:34\U52>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Next/STATIONARY/FullPlanned.lean#L34-L52>
  connects the action data to the auxiliary logarithmic estimate.
  <hlink|<verbatim|YM/Next/STATIONARY/Level/Transition.lean:153\U178>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Level/Transition.lean#L153-L178>
  then uses <hlink|<verbatim|pole_reduced>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Level/Transition.lean#L153-L178>
  to transfer that estimate to the stationary coefficient; this is a separate
  comparison. B-RG-I p.297, Eqs.(5.37)\U(5.42), extracts the marginal
  coefficient, but Theorem 2, p.259, postpones the promised running-coupling
  proof; B-Large-II p.355 retains the assumption. Abbott82 Ÿ3.3, p.48,
  Eqs.(3.3.1)\U(3.3.5), directly displays the older vector/ghost coefficient;
  Gross\UWilczek and Politzer 1973 supply its historical asymptotic-freedom
  setting. N2's different spin coefficients in Ÿ6, pp.56\U61, are not the
  numerical input for Yang\UMills.

  <strong|Classification.> STANDARD/ADAPTED-OTHER perturbation theory 45%,
  ADAPTED-BALABAN extraction 30%, candidate-NEW controlled matching 25%;
  medium-high confidence. The usual beta-function coefficient
  <math|b<rsub|0>=11*C<rsub|A>/<around|(|48*\<pi\><rsup|2>|)>> is not new
  physics. Lean's <math|\<kappa\><rsub|G>=2*b<rsub|0>=11*C<rsub|A>/<around|(|24*\<pi\><rsup|2>|)>>
  is the corresponding slope for the inverse-square coupling; these
  conventions must not be confused. Completing its uniform linkage to this
  particular exact transformation is a substantial constructive obligation; a
  complete mathematical verification of that linkage remains outside the
  scope of this comparison.

  MRS93 p.376 also describes one-/two-loop flow calculations with next-order
  remainder control and higher-order truncation of gauge changes; ŸVIII
  pp.376\U378 ties coupling relations to Slavnov identities. This is an older
  four-dimensional gauge marginal-control programme. It does not identify the
  matrices or normalization of the particular Lean transfer at
  <hlink|<verbatim|YM/Next/STATIONARY/Level/Transition.lean:153\U178>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Next/STATIONARY/Level/Transition.lean#L153-L178>;
  that bridge remains a separate technical question.

  <subsection|14. Connected activities, compulsory inventories and complete
  supports \V <hlink|III.8|outline/units/III-8.tm>><label|14-connected-activities-compulsory-inventories-and-complete-supports--iii8>

  <strong|Function and size.> 4,103 lines. Only empty-inventory connected
  components may be exponentiated into regular errors. Seeded components
  retain mandatory coverage, and dependence supports include negative status
  queries and all geometric choices.

  <strong|Evidence.> <hlink|<verbatim|YM/RG/Activities.lean:42\U55>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/RG/Activities.lean#L42-L55>,
  <hlink|<verbatim|YM/RG/Activities.lean:77\U96>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/RG/Activities.lean#L77-L96>,
  <hlink|<verbatim|YM/RG/Activities.lean:113\U135>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/RG/Activities.lean#L113-L135>
  records inventory, eligibility, whole-label transport and exact coverage.
  <hlink|<verbatim|YM/SectorNext/VACUUM_NORMALIZATION/Gas.lean:213\U240>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/SectorNext/VACUUM_NORMALIZATION/Gas.lean#L213-L240>
  gives the unforced catalog and the exact deleted-support gas correction by
  omitted logarithmic pieces, supplying the reassembly evidence beyond those
  definitions. N2 Eqs.(5.7)\U(5.10), pp.40\U41, Ÿ5.4, p.49, and Appendix C
  have the closest full representation and reassembly discipline. B-RG-II
  pp.2\U4, Eqs.(1.2)\U(1.8), and B-N-Loc-I ŸŸ2\U4 already localize nonlinear
  background dependence. B-N-II p.676 explicitly demands that local outputs
  depend only on local inputs.

  <strong|Classification.> Mixed ADAPTED-OTHER (GK), ADAPTED-BALABAN and
  ADAPTED-NLSM, with STANDARD support logic. High confidence in the specific
  older covering device; medium in N2 as the closest complete format. GK85
  p.212 Eq.(4.8) already sums disjoint supports covering the bad region, each
  meeting it in a nonempty union of components. Its pp.218\U221, especially
  p.219 Eqs.(5.34)\U(5.39), groups components touching that region and
  exponentiates the outside sum. Mandatory coverage and this selective
  reassembly therefore cannot independently distinguish N2. Lean adds
  explicit inventory labels, eligibility predicates and exact read supports;
  the complete clipped/masked/tagged format remains closer to N2. Complete
  read supports are an exact independence requirement, not a new principle of
  locality. Gauge routes, frames and windows enlarge those supports beyond
  spin-field arguments.

  <subsection|15. Exact coupling reset and restoration of the activity class
  \V <hlink|III.9|outline/units/III-9.tm>><label|15-exact-coupling-reset-and-restoration-of-the-activity-class--iii9>

  <strong|Function and size.> 7,162 lines. The marginal and vacuum pieces are
