  <subsection|16. Energy per seed and protection of rough sectors \V
  <hlink|III.10|outline/units/III-10.tm> (a)><label|16-energy-per-seed-and-protection-of-rough-sectors--iii10-a>

  <strong|Function and size.> Within <hlink|III.10|outline/units/III-10.tm>'s
  49,766 lines. Energy reserved for primary rough seeds pays entropy,
  normalization and derivative costs without repeatedly spending the same
  reserve. Protecting complete neighborhoods prevents local expansions from
  erasing the predicates that selected the sector.

  <strong|Evidence.> <hlink|<verbatim|YM/Pressure/Seeds.lean:22\U58>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Pressure/Seeds.lean#L22-L58>,
  <hlink|<verbatim|YM/Pressure/Seeds.lean:124\U131>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Pressure/Seeds.lean#L124-L131>
  records three inventories and the energy lower bound per share.
  <hlink|<verbatim|YM/Next/FLUCTUATIONS/Grants.lean:24\U36>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Next/FLUCTUATIONS/Grants.lean#L24-L36>
  supplies those bounds and controls their costs in the stage order. N2 Lemma
  5.2, pp.43\U44, p.45 and Appendix C use primary cores, protector supports
  and energy reserves in the same retained-density context. B-Conv Ÿ2,
  pp.254\U262, and B-Large-I pp.175\U177 give the older need to keep and
  repeatedly control large-field regions.

  <strong|Classification.> ADAPTED-NLSM 45%, ADAPTED-BALABAN 30%, specialized
  adaptation 25%; medium-high confidence. YM seeds include bad plaquettes and
  incompatible coarse bonds, not just large spin gradients. The
  super-polylogarithmic monitor and gauge chart costs change the quantitative
  balance. Balaban's separate aged-region R replacement was not identified as
  a literal transformation in these interfaces.

  MRS93 p.376 supplies another older protection mechanism: asymmetric
  corridors toward lower frequencies distribute a large-field saving over
  additional boxes and compensate high/low coupling costs. GK85 p.222
  Eq.(6.5) retains bad-region energy and entropy in the inductive bound.
  These strengthen older ancestry of protected rare-region reserves; the Lean
  inventory/support geometry and its particular reserve schedule remain
  distinct.

  <subsection|17. Nonlinear contraction and bounds on irrelevant terms \V
  <hlink|III.10|outline/units/III-10.tm> (b)><label|17-nonlinear-contraction-and-bounds-on-irrelevant-terms--iii10-b>

  <strong|Function and size.> Also within
  <hlink|III.10|outline/units/III-10.tm>. The exact step is reorganized so
