  <hlink|<verbatim|YM/Source/Construction.lean:65\U72>|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Source/Construction.lean#L65-L72>
  preserves the normalization and translations without retuning. N2 Ÿ7,
  pp.61\U65, and N3 Ÿ6, pp.55\U60, provide the closest terminal-coupling
  trajectory organization. B-RG-I Theorem 2, p.259, expresses the older
  tuned-coupling objective; B-N-II Theorem 1, p.680, provides a complete
  iterative framework in a different model.

  <strong|Classification.> ADAPTED-NLSM 35%, ADAPTED-BALABAN 20%, STANDARD
  assembly 35%, specialized extension 10%; medium confidence. A long formal
  iteration proof is not a corresponding quantity of new physical ideas.
  Serving all spin moments with one trajectory is already present in N3; the
  added obligations here are the larger gauge-composite and derivative
  comparison systems.

  <subsection|24. Activity costs, local observable derivatives and analytic
