    Background Fields in Renormalization Group Method for Lattice Gauge
    Theories,\Q <em|Communications in Mathematical Physics> <strong|102>
    (1985), 277\U309. <hlink|DOI|https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01229381>. Read
    pp.277\U286,292\U300,305\U309, especially Theorem 1 and Propositions 6,9;
    omitted calculations at p.308 are noted.

    <item><strong|GK85.> Krzysztof Gaw¦dzki and Antti Kupiainen, \PMassless
    Lattice \<varphi\>\<#2074\>\<#2084\> Theory: Rigorous Control of a
    Renormalizable Asymptotically Free Model,\Q <em|Communications in
    Mathematical Physics> <strong|99> (1985), 197\U252.
    <hlink|DOI|https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01212281>. Read
    pp.197\U201,207\U213,217\U222,233\U234,236\U237,245\U246: compulsory
    covering, selective reassembly, marginal extraction, constant order and
    critical mass tuning. This is scalar <strong|infrared> asymptotic
    freedom.

    <item><strong|Seiler82.> Erhard Seiler, <em|Gauge Theories as a Problem
    of Constructive Quantum Field Theory and Statistical Mechanics>, Lecture
    Notes in Physics <strong|159>, Springer, 1982. Introduction, lattice and
    continuum parts and geometric appendix available. Read contents and
    introductory framework, Ÿ2a pp.12\U16 and beginning Ÿ2b pp.16\U17, Ÿ5a
    pp.99\U103, selected Ÿ6b pp.118\U121 and Ÿ6c\Ud p.130 onward. The
    appendix was available but not substantively used; later continuum
    chapters were not read in full. Theorems 2.1\U2.2 supply reflection
    positivity/chessboard context; Ÿ6b concerns matter determinants in
    external fields and explicitly labels its four-dimensional statement
    Quasi-Theorem 6.10. No matching pure-gauge torus count was located.
  </itemize-minus>

  <subsection|7.5 Background references and unread
  originals><label|75-background-references-and-unread-originals>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><strong|Wilson74 \V established background; not directly read.>
    Kenneth G. Wilson, \PConfinement of quarks,\Q <em|Physical Review D>
    <strong|10> (1974), 2445\U2459. The gauge-link/plaquette lattice
    formulation is the background result cited; no unverified equation number
    is supplied. Directly read evidence for its use in this tradition is
    B-RG-I p.252 Eq.(0.2), which credits Wilson.

    <item><strong|Glimm\UJaffe87 \V established background; not directly
    read.> James Glimm and Arthur Jaffe, <em|Quantum Physics: A Functional
    Integral Point of View>, second edition, Springer, 1987. No specific
    unread theorem or chapter is evidence for a distinctive correspondence.
  </itemize-minus>

  Seiler82 and the five 1985 Baªaban gauge papers are directly read sources
  in Ÿ7.4. Osterwalder\USeiler 1978 and Zimmermann 1973 remain unavailable in
  full, with abstract-only entries there. Names listed in Ÿ6 as further
  literature comparisons are not additional sources silently used here.
  Direct reading, partial reading, abstract-only access and background
  knowledge must remain distinguishable.

  <section|Source keys><label|source-keys>

  Full publication details and reading limits are in
  <hlink|Ÿ7|#7-bibliography-and-source-access>. NLSM means nonlinear sigma
  model; RG means renormalization group; UV means ultraviolet.

